          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "<em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "</em>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0147",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]Example 1: To create a maintenance window[[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "<strong>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "</strong>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0148",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The following [[p0]] example creates a new maintenance window that every five minutes for up to two hours (as needed), prevents new tasks from starting within one hour of the end of the maintenance window execution, allows unassociated targets (instances that you haven’t registered with the maintenance window), and indicates through the use of custom tags that its creator intends to use it in a tutorial.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "create-maintenance-window"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0149",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Output:",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0150",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For more information, see [[p0]] in the [[p1]]AWS Systems Manager User Guide[[p2]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Tutorial: Create and configure a maintenance window using the AWS CLI"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "<em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "</em>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0151",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]Example 2: To create a maintenance window that runs only once[[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "<strong>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "</strong>"
        }
